d, and this move left Black well behind."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "The 14k's C5 lost 29.8 points, the biggest swing of the game, moving Black's lead from -22.1 to +7.7. The engine wanted E4 there. By move 29 the board shows Black has captured 5 stones, and the game was suddenly open."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "With a lead of +13.2, Opus 5.5 played G4 and lost 14.6 points, dropping to -1.4. The engine's choice was F7. It was Black's worst move of the game, and it undid the swing Black had gained."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "F7, the engine's own choice, lost only 0.2 points and held Black's lead at +9.5. The engine had named F7 over several earlier turns, so Black had to wait before playing it."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "E5 lost 9.1 points and turned a lead of +3.4 into -5.7. The engine preferred D7. Black never got back above -5 after this, and the closing moves barely changed the score."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py applies one named move and reports captures and group liberties, libs.py lists groups and their liberties, and count.py counts stones and enclosed territory on a pasted board; none of them loops over candidate moves or plays out continuations, so they only inspect the current position.", "stop": false}}